// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: method `dup` has no receiver — add `&self`/`&var self`, or declare it `static func` if a static was intended
//
// Design 236, position-matrix row 1: a self-less non-`init` `func` in a
// STRUCT extension. Staticness was fully determined by the missing receiver,
// so it used to be inferred — and the V39 incident (Aug 17) showed the
// inference converting an authoring MISTAKE into a different kind of method:
// this exact shape, `func dup(x: T)` written meaning an instance method with
// the `&self` forgotten, became a static that only resolved through a broken
// call path. The keyword turns forgot-`&self` into the right error at the
// declaration, and the fixit names both readings because the compiler cannot
// know which one was meant.

struct Bag { n: Int }

extension Bag {
    func dup(x: Int) -> Int { x * 2 }
}

func main() { print("unreached") }
